    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0427" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War, 1939/88: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-03T12:00:00+01:00">September 3,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1031. My 1024, September 3, 9 a.m. The French Ambassador has just left for the
                    Foreign Office to present a note to Ribbentrop<anchor n="26" xml:id="d421-f1"/>
                    stating that inasmuch as the German Government has not replied to the French
                    note of September 1 the French Government will take steps as of 5 o’clock this
                    afternoon to fulfill its agreement with Poland. Fuller statement of note
                    follows.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
